# ==============================================================================
# local.sgdc — this stage's own SGDC, appended after the specification seed and
# the generated constraint-annotations block. The only SGDC file you edit, and
# the only one carried into the next round.
#
# What belongs here: port/clock associations the seed cannot know, and analysis
# scope you decided on. What does NOT: clocks, resets and their polarity (the
# seed's — a correction goes to specification and arrives here on its own), and
# anything in constraint-annotations.json (generated — a wrong entry is its
# author's to fix, and this stage's failure routing sends it there).
# ==============================================================================

# Reset port association — bind a reset to the domain it resets.
#   abstract_port -ports <rst> -clock <clk> -reset <rst>
#
# Input port clock association — bind an input to its driving domain, so CDC
# recognises the driver side of a crossing.
#   abstract_port -ports <port> -clock <clk>
